  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reduce Tensions and Strengthen Social Cohesion between Returnees and Host Communities through Access to Identity Documents, Livelihoods and the Transitional Justice Process</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to prevent violence and strengthen social cohesion between returnee populations and the communities residing in their host or home areas, by addressing the causes of tension between the two communities. The project has structured its approach and interventions around the administrative, social and economic obstacles hindering the resettlement of returnees and their peaceful reintegration into their home or host communities. The project&apos;s interventions will focus on 3 complementary strategic objectives, which aim to i) create the necessary conditions for the administrative regularization of returnees/repatriates to facilitate their reintegration in their rights (identity documents, land titles, etc.) including rights related to housing, land and property (LTB) issues; ii) to strengthen inter-community links by reinforcing economic ties within communities and iii) to facilitate the inclusion of returnees in the transitional justice process to help combat prejudice and reduce the desire for revenge.</narrative>
  </description>
